The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Removed set_window() calls in tce_iommu_take_ownership_ddw()
table_group->ops->take_ownership(table_group);
```
Reason:
The removal of the `set_window()` calls in the `tce_iommu_take_ownership_ddw` function meant that when a new group was attached to a container that already had IOMMU tables, the necessary programming of those tables to the hardware was not performed. This broke the functionality required for VFIO PCI hotplug.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < IOMMU_TABLE_GROUP_MAX_TABLES; ++i) {
    struct iommu_table *tbl = container->tables[i];
    ret = table_group->ops->set_window(table_group, i, tbl);
}
```
Reason:
The added loop iterates over the IOMMU tables in the container and calls `set_window()` for each table, ensuring that the IOMMU tables are properly programmed to the hardware when a new group is attached. This restores the functionality that was lost due to the previous commit.

